1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:04,332
AI agents can now shop and pay on behalf of a business.

2
00:00:04,702 --> 00:00:09,126
But one line hidden in a supplier listing can hijack them. And when a delivery

3
00:00:09,146 --> 00:00:11,690
comes up short, nobody claims the money back.

4
00:00:12,910 --> 00:00:18,419
This is GuardedBuyer, a buyer-side purchasing agent built on PayPal and AP2

5
00:00:18,439 --> 00:00:19,082
mandates.

6
00:00:19,452 --> 00:00:24,288
An LLM reads the request and compares supplier quotes. Deterministic code

7
00:00:24,308 --> 00:00:26,416
decides whether any money moves.

8
00:00:27,636 --> 00:00:32,400
An employee asks for two laptops: twenty-two hundred dollars, against fifteen

9
00:00:32,420 --> 00:00:34,264
hundred left in the IT budget.

10
00:00:34,634 --> 00:00:39,402
The agent tries to pay anyway. The payment is refused and logged, because the

11
00:00:39,422 --> 00:00:41,454
agent has no approve tool at all.

12
00:00:41,824 --> 00:00:46,117
The approver sees why it was blocked, the chosen quote, and the exact limits

13
00:00:46,137 --> 00:00:47,252
that will be signed.

14
00:00:48,472 --> 00:00:51,860
The manager approves with a note, then finance approves.

15
00:00:52,230 --> 00:00:56,767
Release signs a fresh AP2 Intent Mandate that pins the merchant, item,

16
00:00:56,787 --> 00:01:01,258
quantity and maximum amount, and verifies it before PayPal is called.

17
00:01:02,478 --> 00:01:07,512
Release creates a real order on the PayPal sandbox through Orders v2. That is

18
00:01:07,532 --> 00:01:08,890
its sandbox order ID.

19
00:01:09,260 --> 00:01:13,773
A sandbox buyer would approve it on PayPal. Here, PayPal's sandbox test card

20
00:01:13,793 --> 00:01:15,264
stands in for that click.

21
00:01:15,634 --> 00:01:20,131
The agent reads the order back, checks it against the mandate, and only then

22
00:01:20,151 --> 00:01:23,222
captures. The capture ID comes straight from PayPal.

23
00:01:24,442 --> 00:01:24,502
Back in the offline emulation, a delivery comes up short: three toner

24
00:01:24,522 --> 00:01:24,542
cartridges arrive instead of four.

25
00:01:24,912 --> 00:01:29,687
The agent reconciles the delivery and drafts a PayPal dispute for exactly the

26
00:01:29,707 --> 00:01:32,116
missing amount, with a factual message.

27
00:01:32,486 --> 00:01:36,988
Buyers can't open disputes through the API, so a person files the draft, and

28
00:01:37,008 --> 00:01:39,666
the agent tracks it through the Disputes API.

29
00:01:40,886 --> 00:01:45,451
Next, a poisoned listing with a fake system notice, and a fully compromised

30
00:01:45,471 --> 00:01:46,674
agent that obeys it.

31
00:01:47,044 --> 00:01:51,382
It tries to approve itself, switch to the attacker's store, and order four

32
00:01:51,402 --> 00:01:55,505
hundred units. Every attempt is blocked, and the real order still goes

33
00:01:55,525 --> 00:01:55,976
through.

34
00:01:57,196 --> 00:02:01,712
We measured this on two hundred synthetic requests, each run three ways.

35
00:02:02,082 --> 00:02:06,903
Full guardrails stopped ninety-one of ninety-six attack cases. A classic spend

36
00:02:06,923 --> 00:02:11,062
policy stopped sixty. Neither blocked a single legitimate purchase.

37
00:02:11,432 --> 00:02:14,532
The five misses are listed openly, one click away.

38
00:02:15,752 --> 00:02:20,122
The same client passes a smoke test against the real PayPal sandbox:

39
00:02:20,142 --> 00:02:25,092
idempotent create, the not-approved path, capture, and a safe second capture.

40
00:02:26,312 --> 00:02:30,564
GuardedBuyer. Let AI do the buying, without handing it the keys.
